#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""ethproofs-mock — a home-made, plug-compatible stand-in for the ethproofs.org submission API.

The real ethproofs clients (RSP `bin/eth-proofs`, ZisK `zisk-ethproofs`) POST proofs to an ethproofs
endpoint. Until we have real ethproofs.org credentials, point those clients' ETHPROOFS_API_URL /
--eth-proofs-endpoint at THIS server: it implements the same surface, records every submission,
VERIFIES + saves each proof, and serves a leaderboard-like status page. So the full continuous pipeline
(chain-follow -> witness -> prove on the cluster -> submit) runs end-to-end NOW, and swapping to the
real ethproofs.org later is a one-line config change (URL + token) — zero pipeline change.

Like the real server, this one VERIFIES the proof on /proved (it's the trust anchor, not a dumb store).
A stdlib server can't run the SP1/ZisK verifier, so by default it MOCK-verifies (structural: a real,
non-empty, decodable proof carrying a verifier id + a block) and records a ✓/✗ verdict. Swap in a REAL
verifier with --verify-cmd `<cmd> <proof_path> <block> <verifier_id>` (exit 0 = valid) — the verification seam.

Endpoints (mirrors what the clients call). Proof identity is (cluster_id, block) — exactly as on
ethproofs — so run each prover as its OWN cluster (cli/prove-farm defaults the cluster to the guest, so
rsp vs zisk land on distinct clusters). Optional vm/guest/public_inputs (sent by cli/ethproofs-submit)
identify WHAT was proven and show on the leaderboard:
  POST /proofs/queued   {block_number, cluster_id, [vm, guest]}
  POST /proofs/proving  {block_number, cluster_id, [vm, guest]}
  POST /proofs/proved   {proof (base64), block_number, proving_cycles|proving_steps, proving_time (ms),
                         verifier_id, cluster_id, [vm, guest, public_inputs, t_block, e2e_secs]}
                         -> verified, returns {proof_id, verified}
  GET  /                 leaderboard (HTML: pipeline banner + cluster·vm·guest·block·verified)
  GET  /proofs           JSON records   ·   GET /status   JSON pipeline state

Plus ONE endpoint the real ethproofs.org does not have, because only the producer knows it:

  POST /status          {chain_tip, [last_witness, queue_files, cluster_id, vm, guest, source]}

The three lifecycle POSTs above say what happened to ONE proof; they cannot say where the pipeline is as
a whole, and above all nobody tells this server what the CHAIN's head is — so "how far behind are we?",
the question that decides whether proving is real-time, is unanswerable from proof records alone. A
producer (the witness follower) heartbeats POST /status with the tip it is following; GET /status and the
leaderboard banner then answer, per pipeline: tip → last witness → block being proved → last proved →
**last verified**, with the lag in blocks (and an estimate in seconds at 12 s/slot).

Lenient by design (a stand-in): unknown/renamed fields are still recorded; any Bearer token is
accepted unless --token is given. Verification is mock by default (a real, well-formed proof passes).

  ./cli/ethproofs-mock [--port 8547] [--store <dir>] [--token <expected-bearer>] [--verify-cmd <cmd>]

Store (default: ethproofs-mock-data/ at the repo root, git-ignored): submissions.jsonl (append log,
replayed on restart) + proofs/<cluster>-<block>.bin (the decoded proofs).
"""
import argparse, base64, json, os, subprocess, sys, threading
from http.server import BaseHTTPRequestHandler, ThreadingHTTPServer
from datetime import datetime, timezone

ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
MOCK_MAGIC = b"MOCK-PROOF"   # prove-farm --mock writes proof bytes starting with this — a fake, never real

def now_iso():
    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")

class Store:
    """Append-only submission log + per-(cluster,block) latest state, rebuilt on restart."""
    def __init__(self, d):
        self.dir = d
        self.proofs_dir = os.path.join(d, "proofs")
        self.jsonl = os.path.join(d, "submissions.jsonl")
        self.status_path = os.path.join(d, "status.json")
        os.makedirs(self.proofs_dir, exist_ok=True)
        self.lock = threading.Lock()
        self.state = {}          # (cluster, block) -> latest record (no proof blob)
        self.ids = {}            # (cluster, block) -> stable proof_id
        self.next_id = 1
        self.pipelines = {}      # cluster (or "*") -> last producer heartbeat (POST /status)
        self._replay()
        self._load_status()

    def pid(self, cluster, block):
        # Stable proof_id per (cluster, block) — the SAME identity ethproofs uses. Run each prover as its
        # own cluster so rsp vs zisk don't share a key (cli/prove-farm defaults the cluster to the guest).
        # The real ethproofs API returns {"proof_id": N}; the ZisK client PARSES it (RSP ignores it).
        key = (cluster, block)
        with self.lock:
            if key not in self.ids:
                self.ids[key] = self.next_id
                self.next_id += 1
            return self.ids[key]

    def _replay(self):
        if not os.path.exists(self.jsonl):
            return
        with open(self.jsonl) as f:
            for line in f:
                line = line.strip()
                if not line:
                    continue
                try:
                    r = json.loads(line)
                    self.state[(r.get("cluster_id"), r.get("block_number"))] = r
                except json.JSONDecodeError:
                    pass

    def record(self, event, body, proof_bytes=None, verified=None, verify_reason=None):
        cluster = body.get("cluster_id")
        guest = body.get("guest")
        block = body.get("block_number")
        rec = {
            "ts": now_iso(),
            "event": event,
            "cluster_id": cluster,
            "vm": body.get("vm"),                          # zkVM: SP1 / ZisK / OpenVM
            "guest": guest,                                # guest program: rsp / zisk-reth / monad-sp1 / …
            "mock": body.get("mock"),                      # True = a FAKE proof (mock-cluster), not real
            "block_number": block,
            "public_inputs": body.get("public_inputs"),    # digest — identifies non-block proofs (e.g. fibonacci)
            # work-unit is cycles (SP1/OpenVM) or steps (ZisK) — record whichever is present
            "proving_cycles": body.get("proving_cycles", body.get("proving_steps")),
            "proving_time_ms": body.get("proving_time"),
            # chain time of the block, and chain-time -> our ack: the whole pipeline, node to ethproofs
            "t_block": body.get("t_block"),
            "e2e_secs": body.get("e2e_secs"),
            # Where the non-prover time goes. Kept alongside e2e because e2e alone cannot distinguish a slow
            # pipeline from a slow prover, and that ambiguity cost a day of optimising the wrong term.
            "transport_secs": body.get("transport_secs"),
            "pulled_direct": body.get("pulled_direct"),
            "witness_secs": body.get("witness_secs"),
            "verifier_id": body.get("verifier_id"),
            "proof_bytes": proof_bytes,
            # server-side verdict (the SERVER verifies — see mock_verify). None until /proved.
            "verified": verified,
            "verify_reason": verify_reason,
        }
        with self.lock:
            with open(self.jsonl, "a") as f:
                f.write(json.dumps(rec) + "\n")
            # keep the fullest view: merge into any existing state for this (cluster, block)
            key = (cluster, block)
            prev = self.state.get(key, {})
            merged = {**prev, **{k: v for k, v in rec.items() if v is not None}}
            merged["event"] = event
            merged["ts"] = rec["ts"]
            self.state[key] = merged
        return rec

    # ---- pipeline status: the producer's heartbeat + what the proof records imply ------------------
    def _load_status(self):
        """Survive a restart: the last heartbeat is the only place the chain tip is known."""
        try:
            with open(self.status_path) as f:
                self.pipelines = {k: v for k, v in json.load(f).items()}
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            self.pipelines = {}

    def set_status(self, body):
        """Record a producer heartbeat. Keyed by cluster so several pipelines (rsp / zisk / monad) can
        report side by side; '*' when the producer doesn't name one."""
        key = str(body.get("cluster_id")) if body.get("cluster_id") is not None else "*"
        hb = {
            "ts": now_iso(),
            "cluster_id": body.get("cluster_id"),
            "vm": body.get("vm"),
            "guest": body.get("guest"),
            "source": body.get("source"),               # free-form: who is reporting (e.g. "nyc-003")
            "chain_tip": body.get("chain_tip"),         # the head the producer is following
            "last_witness": body.get("last_witness"),   # newest block a witness exists for
            # framed inputs sitting in the queue — NOT an un-proven backlog (prove-farm leaves proven
            # inputs in place); the backlog signal is the lag below. Legacy name accepted too.
            "queue_files": body.get("queue_files", body.get("queue_depth")),
        }
        with self.lock:
            self.pipelines[key] = hb
            try:
                with open(self.status_path, "w") as f:
                    json.dump(self.pipelines, f, indent=1)
            except OSError:
                pass                                     # status is a convenience, never fatal
        return hb

    def derive(self, cluster=None):
        """Fold the proof records into a per-pipeline position. `cluster=None` folds over everything.
        Every field is a BLOCK NUMBER (or None): where the pipeline currently is."""
        def blocks(pred):
            out = [r.get("block_number") for r in self.state.values()
                   if r.get("block_number") is not None
                   and (cluster is None or str(r.get("cluster_id")) == str(cluster))
                   and pred(r)]
            return max(out) if out else None
        return {
            "proving":  blocks(lambda r: r.get("event") == "proving"),
            "proved":   blocks(lambda r: r.get("event") == "proved"),
            "verified": blocks(lambda r: r.get("verified") is True),
            "rejected": blocks(lambda r: r.get("verified") is False),
            "proofs":   len([r for r in self.state.values()
                             if cluster is None or str(r.get("cluster_id")) == str(cluster)]),
        }

    def status(self):
        """The answer to 'where is the pipeline, and how far behind the chain?' — one entry per
        pipeline. Lags are in blocks; the seconds figure is an ESTIMATE at 12 s/slot, not a measurement
        (a real end-to-end latency needs the producer's own timestamps, single-clock)."""
        keys = list(self.pipelines.keys()) or ["*"]
        out = []
        for k in keys:
            hb = self.pipelines.get(k, {})
            cluster = hb.get("cluster_id")
            d = self.derive(cluster)
            tip = hb.get("chain_tip")
            def lag(b):
                return (tip - b) if (isinstance(tip, int) and isinstance(b, int)) else None
            entry = {
                "cluster_id": cluster, "vm": hb.get("vm"), "guest": hb.get("guest"),
                "source": hb.get("source"), "heartbeat_ts": hb.get("ts"),
                "chain_tip": tip, "last_witness": hb.get("last_witness"),
                "queue_files": hb.get("queue_files"),
                **d,
                "lag_blocks": {"witness": lag(hb.get("last_witness")), "proving": lag(d["proving"]),
                               "proved": lag(d["proved"]), "verified": lag(d["verified"])},
            }
            lv = entry["lag_blocks"]["verified"]
            entry["lag_secs_est"] = lv * 12 if isinstance(lv, int) else None
            # Coverage over the span actually attempted: proofs submitted vs blocks between the first and the
            # last. With a prover slower than the chain most blocks are skipped by design, and that ratio is
            # the honest RTP result — not something to leave implicit in the gaps.
            # Only blocks that reached `proved` count as covered: one stuck at queued/proving is exactly the
            # kind of thing this figure must not flatter.
            blocks = sorted(b for (c, b), r in self.state.items()
                            if b is not None and r.get("event") == "proved"
                            and (cluster is None or str(c) == str(cluster)))
            if len(blocks) >= 2:
                entry.update(cov_proved=len(blocks), cov_span=blocks[-1] - blocks[0] + 1,
                             cov_from=blocks[0], cov_to=blocks[-1])
            e2es = sorted(r["e2e_secs"] for r in self.state.values()
                          if r.get("e2e_secs") is not None
                          and (cluster is None or str(r.get("cluster_id")) == str(cluster)))
            if e2es:
                entry.update(e2e_median=e2es[len(e2es) // 2], e2e_min=e2es[0], e2e_max=e2es[-1])
            out.append(entry)
        return out

    def save_proof(self, cluster, block, proof_b64):
        try:
            raw = base64.b64decode(proof_b64)
        except (ValueError, TypeError):
            return None, False
        path = os.path.join(self.proofs_dir, f"{cluster}-{block}.bin")
        with open(path, "wb") as f:
            f.write(raw)
        return len(raw), raw[:len(MOCK_MAGIC)] == MOCK_MAGIC   # (size, is_mock — magic in the bytes)

STORE = None
TOKEN = None
VERIFY_CMD = None   # external verifier: `<cmd> <proof_path> <block> <verifier_id> <vm> <guest>`, exit 0 = valid

def mock_verify(proof_len, body, proof_path):
    """Stand-in for ethproofs.org's proof VERIFICATION — the SERVER's job (it's the trust anchor, not a
    dumb store). A stdlib server can't run the real SP1/ZisK verifier, so by default we MOCK-verify:
    check the submission is a real, non-empty, decodable proof carrying a verifier id + a block. Set
    --verify-cmd to swap in a REAL verifier (this is the verification seam).

    Returns (ok, reason) where ok is True (verified), False (REJECTED — a real proof that failed) or None
    (not applicable). That third state exists because a DECLARED FAKE is not a verification failure: a
    prove-farm --mock proof carries the MOCK-PROOF magic and arrives with mock:true, so the server knows
    before it tries. Reporting ✗ on those cried wolf on every plumbing run, and a real rejection would have
    been lost in the noise. It is deliberately NOT reported as accepted either — the whole point of the
    magic is that a fake can never pass for real."""
    if body.get("mock"):
        return None, "mock proof — fake by construction, verification not applicable"
    if VERIFY_CMD:
        if not proof_path:
            return False, "no proof to verify"
        # pass vm + guest too, so the verifier can pick the right backend (ZisK/SP1) and locate the ELF.
        try:
            r = subprocess.run([VERIFY_CMD, proof_path, str(body.get("block_number")),
                                str(body.get("verifier_id") or ""), str(body.get("vm") or ""),
                                str(body.get("guest") or "")], capture_output=True, timeout=600)
        except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as e:
            return False, f"verify-cmd error: {e}"
        if r.returncode == 0:
            return True, "verified by --verify-cmd"
        tail = (r.stderr or b"").decode(errors="replace").strip().splitlines()
        return False, f"--verify-cmd rejected (exit {r.returncode}: {tail[-1] if tail else ''})"
    # built-in mock verification (structural — catches empty / truncated / mis-fielded submissions)
    if not proof_len:
        return False, "no proof / empty / undecodable base64"
    if not body.get("verifier_id"):
        return False, "missing verifier_id (vk)"
    if body.get("block_number") is None:
        return False, "missing block_number"
    return True, "mock-verified (well-formed; not cryptographically checked)"

class Handler(BaseHTTPRequestHandler):
    def log_message(self, *a):  # quieter default access log; we print our own lines
        pass

    def _auth_ok(self):
        if not TOKEN:
            return True
        return self.headers.get("Authorization", "") == f"Bearer {TOKEN}"

    def _json_body(self):
        n = int(self.headers.get("Content-Length", 0) or 0)
        raw = self.rfile.read(n) if n else b""
        try:
            return json.loads(raw or b"{}")
        except json.JSONDecodeError:
            return {}

    def _reply(self, code, obj=None, ctype="application/json"):
        payload = (obj if isinstance(obj, (bytes, bytearray))
                   else json.dumps(obj if obj is not None else {"ok": True}).encode())
        self.send_response(code)
        self.send_header("Content-Type", ctype)
        self.send_header("Content-Length", str(len(payload)))
        self.end_headers()
        self.wfile.write(payload)

    def do_POST(self):
        if not self._auth_ok():
            return self._reply(401, {"error": "bad bearer token"})
        body = self._json_body()
        cluster = body.get("cluster_id"); guest = body.get("guest"); block = body.get("block_number")
        vm = body.get("vm"); mock = bool(body.get("mock"))
        # who = vm+guest, so rsp vs zisk on the SAME cluster+block are distinct in the log and the store.
        who = f"{('vm=' + str(vm) + ' ') if vm else ''}{('guest=' + str(guest) + ' ') if guest else ''}"
        mk = "[MOCK] " if mock else ""   # unmissable FAKE-proof marker on every log line
        # Every /proofs/* reply is {"proof_id": N} — the ZisK client parses that shape; RSP ignores it.
        # Log lines are INBOUND requests (← = received): the prover's own status reports, NOT work this
        # server does. 'proving'/'proved' are the CLIENT's lifecycle states — the mock only records them.
        if self.path.rstrip("/") == "/status":
            # Producer heartbeat — the only source for the CHAIN tip (no proof record carries it).
            hb = STORE.set_status(body)
            print(f"{now_iso()}  ← /status          {('[' + str(hb['source']) + '] ') if hb.get('source') else ''}"
                  f"cluster={hb.get('cluster_id')} tip={hb.get('chain_tip')} "
                  f"witness={hb.get('last_witness')} queue={hb.get('queue_files')}")
            return self._reply(200, {"ok": True})
        if self.path.rstrip("/") == "/proofs/queued":
            STORE.record("queued", body); print(f"{now_iso()}  ← /proofs/queued   {mk}cluster={cluster} {who}block={block}")
            return self._reply(200, {"proof_id": STORE.pid(cluster, block)})
        if self.path.rstrip("/") == "/proofs/proving":
            STORE.record("proving", body); print(f"{now_iso()}  ← /proofs/proving  {mk}cluster={cluster} {who}block={block}")
            return self._reply(200, {"proof_id": STORE.pid(cluster, block)})
        if self.path.rstrip("/") == "/proofs/proved":
            pb = None; magic_mock = False
            if body.get("proof"):
                pb, magic_mock = STORE.save_proof(cluster, block, body["proof"])
            if magic_mock and not mock:   # server-detected fake (proof bytes carry the MOCK-PROOF magic)
                mock = True; body["mock"] = True; mk = "[MOCK] "
            proof_path = os.path.join(STORE.proofs_dir, f"{cluster}-{block}.bin") if pb is not None else None
            ok, reason = mock_verify(pb, body, proof_path)   # the SERVER verifies (mock/real via --verify-cmd)
            rec = STORE.record("proved", body, proof_bytes=pb, verified=ok, verify_reason=reason)
            pid = STORE.pid(cluster, block)
            mark = ("verified ✓" if ok is True else
                    f"not verified ⊘ ({reason})" if ok is None else
                    f"REJECTED ✗ ({reason})")
            pi = f" pi={rec['public_inputs']}" if rec.get("public_inputs") else ""
            print(f"{now_iso()}  ← /proofs/proved   {mk}cluster={cluster} {who}block={block}{pi} "
                  f"time={rec['proving_time_ms']}ms work={rec['proving_cycles']} proof={pb}B  → stored proof_id={pid} · {mark}")
            return self._reply(200, {"proof_id": pid, "proof_bytes": pb, "verified": ok, "mock": mock})
        return self._reply(404, {"error": f"unknown endpoint {self.path}"})

    def _banner(self):
        """Where each pipeline is, and how far behind the chain — the RTP question. Reads the producer
        heartbeat (POST /status) for the tip; everything else is folded from the proof records."""
        def n(v, lag=None):
            if v is None:
                return "<span class=s>—</span>"
            return f"<b>{v}</b>" + (f" <span class=s>({lag:+d})</span>" if isinstance(lag, int) else "")
        out = ["<div class=bn>"]
        for p in STORE.status():
            lb = p["lag_blocks"]
            who = " · ".join(str(x) for x in (p.get("cluster_id") or "all clusters",
                                              p.get("vm") or "", p.get("guest") or "") if x)
            head = f"<b>{who}</b>"
            if p.get("source"):
                head += f" <span class=s>via {p['source']}</span>"
            line = (f"{head}<br>chain tip {n(p['chain_tip'])} · witness {n(p['last_witness'], -lb['witness'] if isinstance(lb['witness'], int) else None)}"
                    f" · proving {n(p['proving'], -lb['proving'] if isinstance(lb['proving'], int) else None)}"
                    f" · proved {n(p['proved'], -lb['proved'] if isinstance(lb['proved'], int) else None)}"
                    f" · <span class=d>verified {n(p['verified'], -lb['verified'] if isinstance(lb['verified'], int) else None)}</span>")
            if p.get("rejected") is not None:
                line += f" · <span class=r>rejected {p['rejected']}</span>"
            if p.get("queue_files") is not None:
                line += f" · queue <b>{p['queue_files']}</b> file(s)"
            if p.get("lag_secs_est") is not None:
                line += f" · <span class=s>≈{p['lag_secs_est']}s behind (12s/slot est.)</span>"
            # Coverage, spelled out. The table only lists blocks that were submitted, so the ones the prover
            # skipped are invisible gaps in the numbering — this turns them into a figure.
            if p.get("cov_span"):
                line += (f"<br>coverage <b>{p['cov_proved']}/{p['cov_span']}</b> blocks"
                         f" ({100.0 * p['cov_proved'] / p['cov_span']:.0f}%) over {p['cov_from']}..{p['cov_to']}")
                if p.get("e2e_median") is not None:
                    line += (f" · end-to-end median <b>{p['e2e_median']:.1f}s</b>"
                             f" (min {p['e2e_min']:.1f} / max {p['e2e_max']:.1f})")
            if not p.get("heartbeat_ts"):
                line += ("<br><span class=w>no producer heartbeat — POST /status {chain_tip,…} to show "
                         "the chain tip and the real lag</span>")
            else:
                line += f"<br><span class=s>heartbeat {p['heartbeat_ts']}</span>"
            out.append(f"<div>{line}</div>")
        out.append("</div>")
        return "\n".join(out)

    def do_GET(self):
        if self.path.rstrip("/") == "/proofs":
            return self._reply(200, list(STORE.state.values()))
        if self.path.rstrip("/") == "/status":
            return self._reply(200, {"ts": now_iso(), "pipelines": STORE.status()})
        # leaderboard
        rows = sorted(STORE.state.values(),
                      key=lambda r: (r.get("cluster_id") or 0, str(r.get("vm") or ""),
                                     str(r.get("guest") or ""), r.get("block_number") or 0), reverse=True)
        def td(v): return "" if v is None else v
        def secs(ms): return "" if ms is None else f"{ms / 1000:.1f}"

        def queue_wait(r):
            """Whatever e2e is not witness + transport + prove: the block sat waiting to be picked up.

            Derived rather than measured, and deliberately the LAST column to be derived — the other three are
            each timed at their own source. With --newest-first this is the interesting number: a block the
            prover skipped while newer ones arrived shows a large queue and a normal everything-else, which is
            what separates "the pipeline is slow" from "the prover is saturated".

            Blank unless all three parts are known: a partial sum would attribute the missing part to waiting.
            Negative values are clamped and marked — whole-second phase timings against a 0.1 s e2e can round
            past it, and silently showing 0.0 would hide the rounding rather than admit it.
            """
            e2e, w, t = r.get("e2e_secs"), r.get("witness_secs"), r.get("transport_secs")
            p = r.get("proving_time_ms")
            if None in (e2e, w, t, p):
                return ""
            q = e2e - w - t - p / 1000
            return f"{q:.1f}" if q >= 0 else "~0"
        body = ["<!doctype html><meta charset=utf-8><title>ethproofs-mock</title>",
                "<style>body{font:14px system-ui;margin:2rem}h1{font-size:1.2rem}"
                "table{border-collapse:collapse}td,th{border:1px solid #ccc;padding:4px 8px;text-align:right}"
                "td:first-child,th:first-child,.l{text-align:left}.q{color:#999}.p{color:#c60}.d{color:#080}.r{color:#c00}</style>",
                "<style>.bn{margin:0 0 1rem;padding:.6rem .8rem;border:1px solid #ccc;border-radius:6px;"
                "font:13px ui-monospace,monospace;line-height:1.7}.bn b{font-weight:600}"
                ".bn .s{color:#999}.bn .w{color:#c60}</style>",
                f"<h1>ethproofs-mock — {len(rows)} proof(s)</h1>",
                self._banner()]
        body += [
                "<table><tr><th>cluster</th><th class=l>vm</th><th class=l>guest</th><th>mock</th><th>block</th><th class=l>state</th>"
                # Ordered as the block travels: produced, shipped, proved, waited. Every second of e2e lands in
                # one of them, so nothing is left as a remainder for the reader to work out.
                "<th>work-unit</th>"
                "<th>witness (s)</th><th>transport (s)</th><th>prove (s)</th><th>queue (s)</th>"
                "<th>e2e (s)</th><th>proof (B)</th><th>verified</th>"
                "<th class=l>verifier_id</th><th class=l>updated</th></tr>"]
        for r in rows:
            ev = r.get("event", "")
            cls = {"queued": "q", "proving": "p", "proved": "d"}.get(ev, "")
            # Three states, not two: ✓ verified · ✗ REJECTED (a real proof that failed — the alarming one)
            # · ⊘ not applicable (a declared mock). A blank cell means nothing was submitted yet.
            v = r.get("verified")
            ev_proved = r.get("event") == "proved"
            vb = "✓" if v is True else ("✗" if v is False else ("⊘" if ev_proved else ""))
            vc = "d" if v is True else ("r" if v is False else "q")
            blk = td(r.get("block_number")) or (f"pi:{str(r.get('public_inputs'))[:10]}" if r.get("public_inputs") else "")
            body.append(f"<tr><td>{td(r.get('cluster_id'))}</td><td class=l>{td(r.get('vm'))}</td>"
                        f"<td class=l>{td(r.get('guest'))}</td>"
                        f"<td class='r'>{'⚠️MOCK' if r.get('mock') else ''}</td><td>{blk}</td>"
                        f"<td class='l {cls}'>{ev}</td><td>{td(r.get('proving_cycles'))}</td>"
                        # ms is the API's unit; seconds is what a human compares to a 12 s slot.
                        f"<td>{td(r.get('witness_secs'))}</td>"
                        # A dot marks the witness pulled over the direct link rather than pushed through the
                        # tunnel — the difference between ~4 s and ~25 s, and worth seeing per block.
                        f"<td>{td(r.get('transport_secs'))}{'·' if r.get('pulled_direct') else ''}</td>"
                        f"<td>{secs(r.get('proving_time_ms'))}</td>"
                        f"<td>{queue_wait(r)}</td>"
                        f"<td>{td(r.get('e2e_secs'))}</td>"
                        f"<td>{td(r.get('proof_bytes'))}</td>"
                        f"<td class='{vc}' title='{td(r.get('verify_reason'))}'>{vb}</td>"
                        f"<td class=l>{str(td(r.get('verifier_id')))[:18]}</td><td class=l>{td(r.get('ts'))}</td></tr>")
        body.append("</table>")
        return self._reply(200, "\n".join(body).encode(), ctype="text/html; charset=utf-8")

def main():
    global STORE, TOKEN, VERIFY_CMD
    sys.stdout.reconfigure(line_buffering=True)  # live logs even when redirected (`ethproofs-mock &`)
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description="home-made ethproofs.org stand-in")
    ap.add_argument("--port", type=int, default=int(os.environ.get("ETHPROOFS_MOCK_PORT", 8547)))
    ap.add_argument("--store", default=os.environ.get("ETHPROOFS_MOCK_STORE", os.path.join(ROOT, "ethproofs-mock-data")))
    ap.add_argument("--token", default=os.environ.get("ETHPROOFS_MOCK_TOKEN"))
    ap.add_argument("--verify-cmd", default=os.environ.get("ETHPROOFS_MOCK_VERIFY_CMD"),
                    help="external verifier `<cmd> <proof_path> <block> <verifier_id>` (exit 0 = valid); "
                         "omit to use the built-in mock verification")
    args = ap.parse_args()
    STORE = Store(args.store)
    TOKEN = args.token
    VERIFY_CMD = args.verify_cmd
    n = len(STORE.state)
    auth = f"Bearer {TOKEN}" if TOKEN else "open (any token accepted)"
    verify = f"external: {VERIFY_CMD}" if VERIFY_CMD else "built-in mock (well-formed check; real verifier via --verify-cmd)"
    print(f"""ethproofs-mock — a local stand-in for the ethproofs.org API (the SERVER that receives + verifies proofs).
It accepts what a prover submits (POST /proofs/queued · /proving · /proved), VERIFIES each proof, saves
it, and shows a leaderboard — so the proving pipeline can submit here WITHOUT an ethproofs.org account.
It does NOT prove anything: the log lines below are INBOUND requests (← = received) — the prover's own
status reports, so 'proving'/'proved' are the CLIENT's states, not work done by this server. What this
server DOES do on /proved is VERIFY the submitted proof (mock by default — see --verify-cmd) and record ✓/✗.

  listening : http://127.0.0.1:{args.port}     ·  leaderboard: open it in a browser  ·  JSON: GET /proofs
  pipeline  : GET /status (where each pipeline is + lag vs the chain) — the producer feeds it the tip
              with POST /status {{chain_tip, last_witness, queue_files, cluster_id}}
  store     : {args.store}   (submissions.jsonl + proofs/)
  auth      : {auth}     ·  {n} block(s) recorded so far
  verify    : {verify}

To make a prover send its proofs HERE instead of ethproofs.org, set the prover's ethproofs URL to
http://<host>:{args.port}  (<host> = 'localhost' if the prover runs on this machine, else this box's IP):
  · SP1  (bin/eth-proofs)    :  --eth-proofs-endpoint http://<host>:{args.port}
  · ZisK (ethproofs-client)  :  ETHPROOFS_API_URL=http://<host>:{args.port}
  · cli/ethproofs does this for you (its --ethproofs-url defaults here).
Ctrl-C to stop.""")
    try:
        ThreadingHTTPServer(("0.0.0.0", args.port), Handler).serve_forever()
    except KeyboardInterrupt:
        print("\nethproofs-mock: stopped.")

if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
